B.a5J=new A.p4("2. Keep the EA running 24/7 (VPS)","Laptop band ho tab bhi EA chale",'A VPS is a Windows computer in the cloud that never switches off. You rent it monthly (often about $5\u201315).\n\nSteps:\n1) Rent a "Windows VPS" or "Forex VPS" (some brokers give a free VPS above a deposit level: ask your broker first).\n2) Open it from your phone or PC with "Remote Desktop" using the address, user and password the provider sends you.\n3) Inside the VPS: install MetaTrader 5 from your broker and log in with your trading account.\n4) Copy LabeedGoldAI.ex5 into MQL5/Experts, then continue with step 3 below.\n\nAfter that you can close your own laptop: the EA keeps running on the VPS.',null)
B.a5K=new A.p4("1. What you need","Aap ko kya chahiye","\u2022 An MT5 account with a broker that offers gold (XAUUSD). Start with a DEMO account.\n\u2022 MetaTrader 5 running 24 hours a day with the LABEED EA on it.\n\u2022 This app to start, stop and watch the EA.\n\nThe EA only trades while MT5 is open and online. If your PC or laptop is switched off, the EA stops.",null)
B.a5L=new A.p4("3. Connect the EA to this app","EA ko app se jorein",'1) In this app: Accounts > Add account (broker, server, login number, demo/real). No password needed.\n2) Open the account > Connect EA. Copy the EA key id and EA secret (the secret is shown once).\n3) In MT5: Tools > Options > Expert Advisors: tick "Allow algorithmic trading" and "Allow WebRequest", and add the server address shown under Connect EA.\n4) Open a gold chart, set the timeframe to M15, drag LabeedGoldAI onto it and fill in the server address, key id and secret.\n5) Turn on "Algo Trading". Within about 30 seconds the account shows "EA online" here.',null)
B.a5M=new A.p4("5. Demo first","Pehle demo","Run the EA on a demo account for a few weeks and check the results before using real money. Trading gold carries a high risk of loss and no profit is guaranteed.",null)
B.a5N=new A.p4("4. Small account ($50)? Use a Cent account","$50 wale account ke liye Cent account",'On a normal account the smallest gold trade (0.01 lot) moves about $1 per $1 of price, which is far more than 1% of $50, so the EA will correctly refuse to trade.\n\nOpen a "Cent" account with your broker instead (for example Standard Cent). There $50 shows as 5000 cents and the smallest trade is 100 times smaller, so the EA can trade within your risk limit. The EA supports cent accounts.',null)
